    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "==Write a fresh, engaging travel newsletter edition for Zyvox AI, an AI-powered conversational travel planner. Current time: {{ $now.toFormat(\"cccc, LLLL d, yyyy - t\") }}.\n\nHere are the latest REAL travel news headlines, aggregated moments ago from Lonely Planet, Travel + Leisure, Condé Nast Traveler and Skift:\n{{ $json.headlines }}\n\nReturn ONLY the body content (no email headers, no HTML). Structure it in plain text with these clearly labeled sections:\n\nTITLE: a short catchy title for this edition (one line)\nPULSE: a 3-4 sentence \"Destination Pulse\" — summarize in plain English what today's headlines above mean for someone planning a trip. Reference the actual themes from the headlines across the different sources (new routes, visa/entry changes, destination trends, prices, weather/season shifts, festivals, etc). Keep it general and inspiring, NOT a personalized itinerary.\nTIP: one actionable travel-planning tip of the hour (2-3 sentences) — e.g. booking timing, packing, budgeting, documentation, or app-based planning tips.\nCONCEPT: explain one travel-planning concept simply (e.g. shoulder season, layover optimization, travel insurance, visa-on-arrival, points & miles, local currency/tipping norms) in 3-4 sentences\nQUOTE: one inspiring travel quote with its author\nACTION: one small concrete action the reader can take today to move their next trip forward (1 sentence) — e.g. \"Open Zyvox AI and tell it your dream destination to get a personalized itinerary in seconds.\"\n\nKeep it upbeat, practical, and wanderlust-inducing. Do not invent specific prices, flight numbers, or booking links. Keep it general and educational, and where natural, nudge the reader to continue planning inside the Zyvox AI chat.",
        "batching": {}
